A||||8||RossT||first time fiero out this spring, got pulled over@!!!||||14||
Z||000000||RossT||04-15-2001||02:06 AM||||Well, Today I took my fiero out of hibernation to do some routine stuff.  Changes the synchromesh fluid, bled the brakes, clutch, slaves. Changed oil. Finished installing gas tank (bad sending unit) etc etc.  Well it was all together<BR>and I got the urge to take her for a spin.<P>Well no longer than 5 minutes into my test drive a guy in 1 ton ford truck, waves at me and wanted to check out my fiero!!  We spent 10 minute in a parking lot talking about fiero.  His wife even asked me if i wanted to sell.  Thanks, but no thanks!<P>It was nice that someone had good things about a fiero!<P>SPRING IS HERE, SPRING IS HERE,  must be time to put the insurance back on the beast!!||||reg||14
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||04-15-2001||09:22 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by RossT:<BR><B>Well, Today I took my fiero out of hibernation to do some routine stuff.  Changes the synchromesh fluid, bled the brakes, clutch, slaves. Changed oil. Finished installing gas tank (bad sending unit) etc etc.  Well it was all together<BR>and I got the urge to take her for a spin.<P>Well no longer than 5 minutes into my test drive a guy in 1 ton ford truck, waves at me and wanted to check out my fiero!!  We spent 10 minute in a parking lot talking about fiero.  His wife even asked me if i wanted to sell.  Thanks, but no thanks!<P>It was nice that someone had good things about a fiero!<P>SPRING IS HERE, SPRING IS HERE,  must be time to put the insurance back on the beast!!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>When you said "pulled over", I thought of the boys in blue...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||JSocha||04-15-2001||09:29 AM||||Had my GT out yesterday morning and later that evening (thankfully, before the "snow flies" came out for the evening).<P>Took my daughter out in it and then showed and taught her how to drive a stick (My butt cheeks are now relaxed after a good night of drinking).  Have to admit though, she did pretty good as she had a damn good teacher as the co-pilot  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Taught her how to shift without a clutch.<P>She had fun, but didn't want me to know how much.<P>RossT, when you talked about the vehicle pullin out...I started to cringe here as we had a couple of close calls so I was thinking the worst of your GT.<P>Thank goodness she be safe.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jnjsochasig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||87GT||04-15-2001||09:38 AM||||Last week, I had a man walk into my furniture store and asked if the owner of the fiero outside worked there. I said that would be me and what can I do for you?  He asked if I would sell it and I said nope.  He said if I ever did sell it, what would my price be?  I told him that I really didnt have a clue since Ive done a ton of stuff to it lately.  He mentioned that his son saw my car and begged his dad to go down and see if it was for sale.  I thought that was pretty funny.  Anyways, 2 hrs later, I see the same man with another older man stairing at my car and even looking under it and all.  Kinda makes you feel goofy when somebody really likes your car.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Jake_Dragon||04-15-2001||10:42 AM||||Sounds like you had better keep the doors locked.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <BR>Just what are the Laws on someone stalking your car?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
